# ============================================================================
# THE REAL ROOT CAUSE (trace-proven 2026-07-19) — completion starvation via
# compute-USERMODE-ring resolution failure, NOT page-table publication.
# ============================================================================
# On the loser-hang boot (A=124 B=0): the loser's GR channel RANG and the host
# CONSUMED its work (M5.9 exec_doorbell GR gp_get 1->128, client=0xc1d00003; its GR
# TSG GPFIFO_SCHEDULE'd rc=0 st=0). Host GPU went idle (0%) — the compute completed.
# BUT the loser then spins forever in fn=76 ctrl=0x20801702 MC_SERVICE_INTERRUPTS,
# reading interrupt-status regs (BAR0 0xb8101x = 0) — waiting a completion that
# never arrives.
#
# WHY: the loser's completion semaphore is produced by its user-CE channel's
# SEM_RELEASE (CPU-parsed in chan_execute). Its user-CE client 0xc1e0000a wrote its
# finishPayload (va=0x42006c004) only to payload=2 then STOPPED (winner 0xc1e00009
# reached 36). The loser's compute USERMODE channels (gpfifo 0x1210d0000, 0x121010000,
# userd fb=0x3200000) NEVER ring-resolve: chan_exec picked_pdb=0x0 on EVERY attempt.
# They resolve via NEITHER own-PDB (chan_own_pdb returns 0) NOR M5.16 (the global
# 64-entry bar1_wpg MRU only ever holds the KERNEL ring page 0x31f0000 — the loser's
# compute ring loses the MRU race to the winner's + kernel's doubled BAR1 traffic).
# 4b's pin can't help: it needs a prior M5.16 success to seed chans[].gpfifo_phys,
# which never happens for the loser's compute channel. So its final SEM_RELEASE
# never runs -> completion sema stuck -> loser spins in MC_SERVICE_INTERRUPTS.
# The only RING-DARK events are the transient early 0xc1d0000c channel (proc=-1),
# NOT the loser's compute channels — consistent with the task's "PIN=0/DARK=2"
# loser-hang signature, but the cause is compute-ring resolution, not PT publication.
#
